{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":13006958,"ns":0,"title":"Helix angle","extract":"In mechanical engineering, a helix angle is the angle between any helix and an axial line on its right, circular cylinder or cone. Common applications are screws, helical gears, and worm gears.","description":"Angle between a helix and an axial line","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}